+/* A package that cannot target the running title is invisible, not merely
+ * inert. resolve() already refuses activation on a target mismatch, but the
+ * launcher list used to show every installed package - so a player whose
+ * build lacks a given title (e.g. GT2's Combined-disc-only cheats on an
+ * Arcade-only install) saw rows whose toggles silently did nothing. Filter
+ * the listing with the SAME matcher activation uses. game_id and exe hash
+ * are known from init; a target pinned only by disc hash stays hidden until
+ * the disc digest exists (activation would refuse it then anyway). With no
+ * game identity at all (bare runtime), everything stays visible. */
+static bool package_visible_here(const ModPackage& package) {
+    const RuntimeMods& s = state();
+    if (s.game_id.empty()) return true;
+    return target_matches(package, s.game_id, s.exe_sha256, s.disc_sha256);
+}
